       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppaammrrggbbaattooppnngg was obsoleted by ppaammttooppnngg(1), introduced with Netpbm 10.70
       (June 2015).  ppaammttooppnngg is backward compatible with  ppaammrrggbbaattooppnngg,  plus
       adds a plethora additional functions.

       Starting in Release 10.70, ppaammrrggbbaattooppnngg is just an alias for ppaammttooppnngg.

       ppaammrrggbbaattooppnngg was added to Netpbm in 2005, and was always expected to be
       retired eventually because it had almost no features, compared  to  the
       more popular and much older ppnnmmttooppnngg.  It had, in fact, no command line
       options.  But the one feature it had that ppnnmmttooppnngg lacked was the abil‐
       ity  to  recognize  transparency in a PAM image.  ppaammttooppnngg has that, as
       well as most of the features of ppnnmmttooppnngg.

